{%- comment -%}
  PG R36H Ultra Buyer Photos (2026-09-27): the "Loved by Gamers" photo strip
  for the R36H Ultra page, registered in templates/product.pg-r36h-ultra.json
  only. It is sections/pg-ultra-shots.liquid (the R36S Ultra page's strip)
  with the class prefix pg-uls- renamed pg-hus-, data-uls- renamed data-hus-,
  and its own script, assets/pgx-pg-r36h-ultra-shots.js.

  WHY (owner, 2026-09-27: "just imported reviews for R36H Ultra ... copy the
  review structure of R36S Ultra"). The R36H Ultra page was built with its
  reviews switched on, so pg-landing's rating line, rotating review card and
  review grid, and pg-rev-link's "n verified reviews" line, filled in by
  themselves when Judge.me synced the product (34 reviews, 4.68). The one
  review piece that differed from the R36S Ultra page was the photo strip:
  pg-r36h-ultra-story carries the R36H Pro's strip (data-rhs="shots"), a
  plain snap-scrolling rail that ends at its last photo, where the R36S
  Ultra's loops (the photo set printed five times, the rail kept on the
  middle copy). This section is that looping strip, and while it renders it
  hides the story's own strip, so the page shows one strip, the R36S Ultra's.
  The story's strip is hidden rather than taken out of the story section:
  its script still seats it (twice, in the first half second) and updates
  its pill, and neither needs it to be visible. Both strips read the same
  photos (judgeme.review_widget_data: the photo reviews first, then page
  one) and both need three or more, so they come and go together.

  WHAT IT SHOWS, as on the R36S Ultra. Every photo of every review Judge.me
  has synced for this product, one card per photo, each linking to the
  review grid at the bottom; the stars, name and text are the review's own;
  the pill prints the feed's own average and count, then follows the page's
  rating line once pg-rev-link has rendered it. Nothing while the feed holds
  fewer than three photos.

  WHERE IT SITS. The script seats it in the buy column after the Add to cart
  button (a desktop), or after the last bundle tile; on a phone it takes
  order 6, straight after the tiles' run and ahead of the accordions, the
  same seat the story's strip had.

  NOTE: the photos are served from ae-pic-a1.aliexpress-media.com; these are
  imported supplier reviews, which Judge.me marks verified_buyer: false.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign jm = product.metafields.judgeme.review_widget_data.value -%}
{%- assign jm_all = '' | split: '' -%}
{%- if jm -%}
  {%- if jm.photo_gallery -%}{%- assign jm_all = jm_all | concat: jm.photo_gallery -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if jm.reviews -%}{%- assign jm_all = jm_all | concat: jm.reviews -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign shots = 0 -%}
{%- capture shots_html -%}
{%- assign seen2 = '|' -%}
{%- for r in jm_all -%}
{%- assign key2 = '|' | append: r.uuid | append: '|' -%}
{%- unless seen2 contains key2 -%}
{%- assign seen2 = seen2 | append: r.uuid | append: '|' -%}
{%- if r.body != blank -%}{%- assign r_text = r.body -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign r_text = r.body_html | strip_html | strip -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign r_stars = r.rating | plus: 0 -%}
{%- for pic in r.pictures_urls -%}
{%- assign pic_url = pic.huge | default: pic.original | default: pic.compact | default: pic.small -%}
{%- if pic_url != blank -%}
{%- assign shots = shots | plus: 1 -%}
<a class="pg-hus-shot" href="#pg-reviews">
  <img src="{{ pic_url }}" alt="Customer photo from {{ r.reviewer_name | default: 'a verified buyer' | escape }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" width="400" height="500">
  <span class="pg-hus-cap">
    <span class="st">{%- for s in (1..5) -%}{%- if s <= r_stars -%}&#9733;{%- else -%}&#9734;{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}</span>
    <span class="nm">{{ r.reviewer_name | default: 'Verified buyer' | escape }}</span>
    {%- if r_text != blank -%}<span class="tx">{{ r_text | escape }}</span>{%- endif -%}
  </span>
</a>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- if shots > 2 -%}
{%- assign hus_avg = jm.average_rating | times: 1.0 | round: 1 -%}
<style>
  /* the story's own strip (pg-r36h-ultra-story, data-rhs="shots"): replaced by
     this one on this page, see the note at the top */
  #pgx [data-rhs="shots"]{display:none !important}
  /* the strip: the Pro page's rules, renamed. min-width:0 and overflow:hidden
     keep a horizontal scroller from widening the buy column (pg-page-polish
     does the same for the Pro's strip). */
  #pgx .pg-hus-shots{margin:16px 0 4px;min-width:0;max-width:100%;overflow:hidden;font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif}
  #pgx .pg-hus-shots-h{display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:flex-end;gap:10px;margin:0 2px 9px}
  /* under the headline the caption keeps only its "Swipe" hint, right-aligned;
     the BUYER REVIEWS words read as a second title and are hidden */
  #pgx .pg-hus-shots-h b{display:none;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#fff}
  #pgx .pg-hus-shots-h span{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#C79BEA;white-space:nowrap}
  /* the "loved by" header over the photo rail: our purple pill with the page's
     own rating and review count, the purple gradient second line. No invented
     customer counts. */
  #pgx .pg-hus-loved{text-align:center;margin:30px 0 6px}
  #pgx .pg-hus-loved-pill{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#7A2FA2,#9B4BC4 55%,#B478E0);color:#fff;font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.02em;line-height:1;box-shadow:0 12px 26px -14px rgba(155,75,196,.9)}
  #pgx .pg-hus-loved-pill .st{font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.08em}
  #pgx .pg-hus-loved h3{margin:12px 0 0;font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:27px;line-height:1.1;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#fff}
  #pgx .pg-hus-loved h3 span{display:block;background:linear-gradient(100deg,#F3E8FF 0%,#D9B3F5 30%,#B06CE8 60%,#8B3FB8 100%);-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent}
  /* the rail loops (the set is printed five times; the script keeps the rail on
     the middle copy). It does not scroll by itself. Cards are a fixed width:
     cqw is 46% of the rail where container units work, 44vw the fallback. */
  #pgx .pg-hus-rail{overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;overscroll-behavior-x:contain;container-type:inline-size;
    scrollbar-width:none;-ms-overflow-style:none;margin:0 -2px;padding:0 2px 4px}
  #pgx .pg-hus-rail::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
  #pgx .pg-hus-track,#pgx .pg-hus-set{display:flex;gap:10px;width:max-content}
  #pgx .pg-hus-shot{flex:0 0 auto;width:min(210px,44vw);width:min(210px,46cqw);display:block;text-decoration:none !important;
    background:#16101F;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;color:#F1EDF7}
  #pgx .pg-hus-shot img{display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/5;object-fit:cover;background:#0D0714}
  #pgx .pg-hus-cap{padding:8px 10px 10px}
  #pgx .pg-hus-cap .st{color:#C79BEA;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.06em;line-height:1}
  #pgx .pg-hus-cap .nm{display:block;margin-top:4px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
  #pgx .pg-hus-cap .tx{margin:3px 0 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.4;color:#CFC4DE;
    display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:3;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden}
  @media (max-width:900px){
    /* on a phone the buy column is a flex column: the strip follows the tiles'
       run (5) and leads the accordions (6), as on the Pro page */
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pg-hus-shots{order:6;margin:6px 0 18px}
  }
</style>
<div id="pg-hus-shots-src" hidden>
  <div class="pg-hus-shots" data-hus="shots">
    <div class="pg-hus-loved"><span class="pg-hus-loved-pill"><span class="st" aria-hidden="true">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span><span data-hus-loved="pill">Rated {{ hus_avg }}/5 &middot; {{ jm.number_of_reviews }} reviews</span></span><h3>Loved by Gamers<span>Just Like You</span></h3></div>
    <div class="pg-hus-shots-h"><b>Buyer Reviews</b><span>Swipe &rarr;</span></div>
    {%- capture shots_clone -%}{{ shots_html | replace: '<a class="pg-hus-shot"', '<a tabindex="-1" class="pg-hus-shot"' }}{%- endcapture -%}
    <div class="pg-hus-rail" data-hus-loop><div class="pg-hus-track"><div class="pg-hus-set">{{ shots_html }}</div><div class="pg-hus-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div><div class="pg-hus-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div><div class="pg-hus-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div><div class="pg-hus-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div></div></div>
  </div>
</div>
<script src="{{ 'pgx-pg-r36h-ultra-shots.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG R36H Ultra Photos", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG R36H Ultra Photos"}]}
{% endschema %}
